\f1\fs22 The Elvi War Cabinet had again been called together for an emergency session to debate possible action in response to the genocide attempt by the PTD. Anger of the entire Elvi nation was focused the CEO and the Directorate of Proactive Euthanasia and Pre-emptive Reciprocity. The Elvi were ready to heat up this cold war.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We have been very lucky.\'94 Said the Minister of Health. \'93Not one death. We must be very grateful to the Blessed Mother and the protection of the Hybrid T-Virus. Many are still gravely ill, but seem to be recovering.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The lack of deaths does not reduce their culpability!\'94 Reminded the Justice Minister. \'93Their intent was clear. Annihilation of us all.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We have already struck back at the PTD.\'94 The High Elvis announced, \'93The Blessed Mother, some little time ago attacked them on our behalf and has caused significant damage. Financial losses are now only rippling through the economy. She has reduced the total wealth of the PTD by 20% and increased our holdings by 500%. Many of our most ardent enemies have been financially ruined. We have reports that the CEO himself is close to bankruptcy and desperate for funds.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They must pay with their lives.\'94 The Minister of War called out from across the table. \'93We have negotiated contracts to purchase arms from our saviour\'92s grandmother. All next generation firepower. They will have nothing the match us.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Until she sells the PTD the same weaponry.\'94 Cracker, the Great Teacher, pointed out. \'93She may be an ally, but a sale is a sale. There are few things more important to the powerful than the bottom line.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We have plans in place, we have the weapons and we have the will.\'94 The Minister of war barked back.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And what do we do after we win?\'94 The High Elvis posed. \'93I don\'92t want to preside over the PTD. Do you? That is a nightmare I wish to avoid. I am only interested in promoting our interests and our culture. It is far better to hit them where is hurts - in the pocket book.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What of the CEO?\'94 The Minister for War wanted some blood to be spilt. He deserves more than mere poverty.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The CEO must answer to the Board of Directors. With the recent spate of bankruptcies the membership of the board has changed considerably and I am assured the majority are sympathetic to our cause.Indeed, some of them are out largest investors. An insolvent CEO will never be allowed to continue.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You are mistaken, High Elvis. For the ultra-wealthy, bankruptcy is a momentary inconvenience.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley joined in. She knew how slippery her people could be. \'93We will need much more than a lack of liquidity to bring him down. Someone will make a deal, prop him up financially and have themselves a puppet. No, we will need to be something the elites will not forgive.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Do we know who his replacement might be?\'94 The Minister of War was not convinced. \'93Better the devil you know.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is my fondest hope it will be Eloise Shakti.\'94 The High Elvis said proudly. \'93She may not be Elvis, but she will do anything to protect our saviour. I expect she will act in self interest, until in conflicts with her vow to protect Richard.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I agree, up to a certain point. I am willing to bet she has her price.\'94 The Great Teacher suggested. \'93I propose no action be taken until the next meeting of the Board of Directors. There is no need for war.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I agree.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley said. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We vote.\'94 The High Elvis said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The vote was close, but The Great Teacher and the Holy Aunt managed to keep the peace in the PTD, at least in the short term. The meeting was adjourned and they all went out for cocktails and a show. After siphoning alcohol at an alarming rate over several hours, a drunken Great Teacher staggered away from the Quarter and slowly traversed half the city to his palace inside Hardy Tower 1. He did not notice the two well dressed goons following.
